# Camera Overlap and the photo markers: the flight map's menu entry, CheckOnClick, over the
# CAMERA_FEEDBACK shots the link keeps (MAV.camerapoints) - GCSViews/FlightData.cs:4115-4196 and
# 4457-4471, ExtLibs/Maps/GMapMarkerPhoto.cs and GMapMarkerOverlapCount.cs, ported in
# crates/mp-gui/src/camera_photos.rs, mapview.rs and fly.rs over mp-link's camera_points.rs and
# mp-georef's ImageProjection.calc.
#
# The claim: each shot is a photo marker with its footprint, the last four footprints drawn;
# Camera Overlap checked puts the overlap count on the map - each 0.0001-degree cell inside the
# footprints rolled under 25 degrees, counted for the footprints that hold it - and unchecked takes
# it off, clearing the markers, which the next update puts back.
#
# Plays the georeferencing recording, whose 25 shots start a minute in, at 10x. Run from the
# repository root:
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-cameraoverlap.gui -- file:testdata/georef/camera.tlog

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 19

# The first shot is a minute into the recording: at 10x it comes in six seconds. The Telemetry
# Logs tab is the thirteenth, so the strip is scrolled to it first, as fly-playback.gui scrolls.
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
click fly-tabs-right
# A click of the strip's arrow can be lost under the harness; the tab is on the strip from 10.
expect fly.tabs.first >= 10
click fly-tab-tlogs
expect fly.tab tabTLogs
click fly-speed10
expect fly.playback.speed x 10

expect fly.camera_overlap false
expect fly.coverage.cells 0
expect fly.photos > 0
expect fly.photos.footprints > 0

# Checked: the count's cells over the footprints, some held by more than one shot.
click map@0.5x0.5:right
click fly-cameraoverlap
expect fly.camera_overlap true
expect fly.coverage.cells > 0
expect fly.coverage.most > 1

# Unchecked: the count gone; the markers cleared and back with the next update.
click map@0.5x0.5:right
click fly-cameraoverlap
expect fly.camera_overlap false
expect fly.coverage.cells 0
expect fly.photos > 0
